          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.298,
            0.443,
            0.321
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1.1 A Lakh Varieties!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.332,
            0.539,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "Eshwarappa is a farmer in Chintamani, a town in Karnataka. He visits the market regularly to buy seeds for his rice field. During one such visit he overheard a conversation between Ramanna and Lakshmamma. Ramanna said, “Earlier our country had about a lakh varieties of rice. Farmers used to preserve different varieties of seeds and use them to grow rice. Now, we only have a handful of varieties. Also,"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.547,
            0.297,
            0.896,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.535,
            0.65,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "farmers have to come to the market to buy seeds”."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.553,
            0.848,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": "Lakshmamma said, “There is a seed bank near my house. So far, they have collected about a hundred indigenous varieties of rice seeds from different places. You can also buy seeds from there.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.614,
            0.388,
            0.849
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.396,
            0.608,
            0.848,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": "You may have heard the word ‘lakh’ before. Do you know how big one lakh is? Let us find out."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.4,
            0.663,
            0.847,
            0.7
          ],
          "content": "Eshwarappa shared this incident with his daughter Roxie and son Estu ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.397,
            0.7,
            0.849,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "Estu was surprised to know that there were about one lakh varieties of rice in this country. He wondered “One lakh! So far I have only tasted 3 varieties. If we tried a new variety each day, would we even come close to tasting all the varieties in a lifetime of 100 years?”"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.423,
            0.828,
            0.69,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": "What do you think? Guess."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.984
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
